Return the removed item budget to the store (MuPDF 1.28.5)

This file modifies MuPDF. The Mervin PDF project added this local fix on
2026-10-23. It is not an upstream backport. Remove it when the pinned MuPDF
release subtracts removed entries from the store size in fz_remove_item.

Explicit removal unlinks and frees the entry, but leaves its byte count in
store->size. Later insertions can evict unrelated cached resources even when
the live entries fit the configured budget. Subtract the removed entry size
under FZ_LOCK_ALLOC, matching the other eviction paths. A missing key still
changes nothing. Both hashed and scanned keys use this accounting path.

diff --git a/source/fitz/store.c b/source/fitz/store.c
--- a/source/fitz/store.c
+++ b/source/fitz/store.c
@@ -677,6 +677,7 @@
 	}
 	if (item)
 	{
+		store->size -= item->size;
 		/* Momentarily things can be in the hash table without being
 		 * in the list. Don't attempt to unlink these. We indicate
 		 * such items by setting item->next == item. */
